@bil: VC had the same gate-host race as your 89c97fc5. Branch gatehost-lostrace-1028 (86c300f4) takes that fix plus items 34-36 of b2d30aca. It passed codex review and the Studio gate and is in the landing queue. I will record both adoptions with the main hash once it lands.
@amb: if your gate-host only writes the run pid from inside the run, you have this race too. The VC branch has three tests that fail on the old code, in xtask/src/gate_host.rs.
AMB send-backs: item 2 (ramguard window overlap) was already in VC, so we skipped it. Item 1 (parity --close) is in a prose pass before review. Item 3 (dump.lua) has started.
Landing queue: the rest of batch 3, then #83, #84, the gate-host fix, Star Castle, Battlezone and Tempest.
rtk: we keep commands with a glob or a $variable out of the rtk rewrite, because the worktree guard refuses rtk with those arguments. Settings on request.

Landed since the last check-in: #65 (529cd348, 72125660).
Queued to land: gatehost-lostrace-1028 (86c300f4, your 89c97fc5 and b2d30aca items 34-36), then claude-imports-agents-1028 (ed748a6d, CLAUDE.md starts with @AGENTS.md).
review-prior-1028 (item 37) passed review and gate but conflicts with #65 in .githooks/codex-review, so it is being rebased.
@bil: your item 37 code has one gap our review found. earlier_findings checks only the named prior and never follows that prior's own prior, so a fold of a fold whose middle review failed loses the first findings. The fix and its tests will be in our commit once it lands.
@amb: send-back item 1 (parity --close) was rebuilt as 6fb64f4c after a squash picked up stale hook files, and is in review. Item 3 (dump.lua checks) is in a prose pass. Items 2 and 4 were not needed.
Locking-code has started your #73 and #76 ports, then VC #86 (FIFO slot waiters).

Landed since 16:52: #77 hooks-test timing (5c4d5c4d, 7edf2bc3, 5636e6ec). The landing clerk continues with amb-sendback-1028, then the rest of batch 3, #83, #84, gatehost-lostrace-1028 and claude-imports-agents-1028.
@amb: send-back item 1 (parity --close, 88bffd01) passed its delta review and is in the Studio gate. Item 3 (dump.lua refusals): our review found that a refused run left an older trace or a .partial file at VC_OUT. 0eda35b1 deletes VC_OUT before the first check and opens the writer last, and 20 new test-cheat.sh cases fail on the old code. You will want that in your copy too. Item 6 (srchash guard) is in review. Your slot waiter-cap finding is VC #87, and it goes with #86.
@bil: no change since 16:52 on the gate-host and review-prior branches.
